  "body": "## Goal\n\nProtective/test branch only. Stable is intentionally left unchanged until runtime testing confirms this does not disturb Vinted flows.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Adds a conservative network-level blocker for the exact advertising/RTB families observed in the visible popup chains: `3lift.com`, `4dex.io`, `adtrafficquality.google`, `doubleclick.net`, `googlesyndication.com`, `openx.net`, `pbstck.com`, and `seedtag.com`.\n- The blocker applies to headed LIVE mode as well as headless jobs, so ad documents/scripts are aborted before their redirect chain can load.\n- Vinted, Cloudflare challenge, hCaptcha, Google reCAPTCHA and gstatic reCAPTCHA traffic remain allowed.\n- Strengthens the existing pre-navigation popup guard:\n  - makes `window.open` difficult for page scripts to replace;\n  - blocks arbitrary named new browsing contexts, not only `_blank`;\n  - respects `<base target>`;\n  - guards imperative `form.submit()` / `requestSubmit()` paths that can bypass the regular `submit` event.\n- Keeps the existing reactive `BrowserContext.onPage()` close as the final fail-safe.\n- Adds emergency kill switch `FLIPBOT_BLOCK_AD_TECH=false` so the network blocker can be disabled without reverting code.\n\n## Safety\n\n- No negotiation/session/filter logic changed.\n- No Vinted domain is blocked.\n- CAPTCHA/challenge infrastructure is explicitly covered by tests as allowed.\n- Unknown/malformed URLs fail open.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdds policy regression coverage for all observed ad-tech domains, lookalike domains, Vinted and challenge traffic, plus stronger popup-script assertions.",
